<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="expansions-like-factors">
  <title>Margin Chicane Method for Like Terms</title>
  <p>Arrange the two binomials vertically. Multiply the leading terms and the constants directly. Put both cross-products in the right margin, add them, then bring the combined middle term back to the answer.</p>
  <me>\begin{aligned}(3x+2)(5x+4)&amp;=15x^2+(10x+12x)+8\\&amp;=15x^2+22x+8.\end{aligned}</me>
  <figure xml:id="margin-chicane-figure">
    <caption>The completed worked example and the unnumbered questions, arranged as on the classroom sheet.</caption>
    <interactive xml:id="margin-chicane-interactive" iframe="https://ronandownes.github.io/maths/apps/margin-chicane/index.html" width="100%" aspect="16:9"/>
  </figure>
  <p><url href="https://ronandownes.github.io/maths/apps/margin-chicane/index.html" visual="Open the complete interactive sheet full screen"/> to see the paths clearly, hide the worked steps, print the page or reveal answers when checking your work.</p>
  <paragraphs xml:id="expansions-like-factors-print">
    <title>Print-friendly mathematical layout</title>
    <p>The six stacks are reproduced here for print and for use when an embedded page is unavailable. The completed calculation is shown above; the remaining calculations are unnumbered.</p>
    <me>\begin{array}{ccc}
\begin{array}{r}3x+2\\[3pt]5x+4\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}7x-2\\[3pt]5x-3\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}11x-5\\[3pt]2x+3\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}\\[3.5em]
\begin{array}{r}13x-5\\[3pt]2x+3\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}5x-2\\[3pt]5x+2\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}3x^2-2\\[3pt]x^2-5\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
\end{array}</me>
  </paragraphs>
</section>
